  "@type": "Dataset",
  "name": "Oceanographic Database (1894-1987) for the Bering Sea",
  "description": "There are about 40,000 oceanographic stations for the period 1894-1987. 3,500 stations are available for the period 1986-1996 from the Pacific Research Oceanographic Institute. Temperature, salinity, oxygen are the major parameters, but some additional measurements of chemical parameters are available.\n\nDeposited content: descriptive metadata only; underlying research data are not included.\n\nPurpose: Investigation of the large-scale variability of environmental conditions of the Bering Sea region. These data are not available for analysis but can be processed in Russia, and results could be published.",
